5
00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:11.730
Okay, well, I would like to play a game with you.

6
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:12.563
Okay.

7
00:00:12.563 --> 00:00:14.593
It's time for "In A Pickle!"

8
00:00:14.593 --> 00:00:18.930
(audience cheering)
(pickle crunching)

9
00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.330
Okay, we're gonna eat some sour pickles

10
00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.070
while I ask you some questions; are you ready for it?

11
00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:25.600
I hope so, yeah.
All right.

12
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.170
First pickle, we're going sour.

13
00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:28.616
Okay.

14
00:00:28.616 --> 00:00:29.450
Okay, ready?

15
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:30.371
All right.

16
00:00:30.371 --> 00:00:31.204
(pickle crunching)
Oh.

17
00:00:31.204 --> 00:00:32.860
(mumbling) Broadway song you can't stop listening to

18
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:33.693
and why.

19
00:00:35.085 --> 00:00:36.435
(coughing) Broadway song?

20
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.640
Oh man, I haven't watched-

21
00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.329
well, no, I watched "Oliver" the other day.

22
00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:45.643
(high-pitched) Mm.
Hadn't seen that in a while.

23
00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.820
So, something from that? I don't know.

24
00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.330
I also like "Rent."

25
00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:51.327
Of course.

26
00:00:51.327 --> 00:00:52.430
"Hamilton's" always on rotation too.

27
00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:53.360
I mean, sure, "Hamilton,"

28
00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:54.280
but that's kind of cliche these days.

29
00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.150
All right, take another bite.

30
00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:55.983
Okay.

31
00:00:55.983 --> 00:00:58.380
You're obsessed with mud larking? What is that?

32
00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.830
Well, it's something I think you would really dig.

33
00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:01.663
Really?
Yeah.

34
00:01:01.663 --> 00:01:05.798
So mud larking, I just stumbled on it on like YouTube.

35
00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:08.560
It's like, these people, they-

36
00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.210
a lot of it happens in London and you know,

37
00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:12.080
there's the Thames.

38
00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.588
And so they like walk along the Thames River

39
00:01:14.588 --> 00:01:18.330
and they find artifacts from medieval times,

40
00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:23.240
from Roman times and you know, old coins, stuff like that;

41
00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.250
that's mud larking.

42
00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.100
All right, next pickle.

43
00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.920
It's a hot and spicy one.

44
00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:27.753
Okay.

45
00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:29.320
Take a bite.

46
00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:30.970
(pickle crunching)

47
00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:33.170
(mumbling) Okay, what's the last lie told?

48
00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:36.783
I love this pickle.

49
00:01:36.783 --> 00:01:39.391
(Drew laughing)
(audience laughing)

50
00:01:39.391 --> 00:01:42.391
(audience clapping)

51
00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:46.750
Ooh, that is spicy though.

52
00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.759
Yeah, no, actually it's not bad.

53
00:01:48.759 --> 00:01:50.300
(Michael laughing)
It's actually really good.

54
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.064
Take another bite.
All right.

55
00:01:52.064 --> 00:01:54.573
(Drew laughing)

56
00:01:54.573 --> 00:01:56.045
(mumbling) If you could go anywhere in the world,

57
00:01:56.045 --> 00:01:57.623
(clear voice) where would it be right now?

58
00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:00.970
I'd love to go to Australia.

59
00:02:02.276 --> 00:02:04.230
(Drew blowing breath out)
New Zealand, that whole area.

60
00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:05.063
Yeah.

61
00:02:05.063 --> 00:02:06.180
Tokyo would be cool.

62
00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.750
I mean, there's a lot of places I haven't been to that...

63
00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.076
Everywhere you named is absolute perfection.

64
00:02:11.076 --> 00:02:11.909
Yeah.

65
00:02:11.909 --> 00:02:13.250
And if anyone has the opportunity to go,

66
00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:14.100
I highly recommend it.

67
00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.268
Okay, finally, chocolate-covered pickle;

68
00:02:16.268 --> 00:02:17.400
(Michael sighing)
this is a first for me.

69
00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.330
Do I have to?

70
00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:21.039
Well, you know, you never know.

71
00:02:21.039 --> 00:02:21.872
(audience laughing)

72
00:02:21.872 --> 00:02:23.840
All right, ready? 1, 2, 3.

73
00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.100
You're stranded on an island

74
00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:27.388
